WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.267
The architecture.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:07.100
A person, a device, an agent, one gate every call goes through, and the tools.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.333
Four zones: the managed device, tool traffic through the tool gateway,

00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:15.300
model traffic through the model gateway,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.433
and the control plane of identity, registry, audit and device policy.

00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:22.967
Start on the managed device.

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:28.233
The end user. Everything starts with a question they ask an agent.

00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:32.633
The AI application, the agent. It is the MCP client.

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:37.933
It asks the model for a plan and calls tools through the proxy.

00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:42.267
Client policy: which MCP servers the client may load.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:45.367
The allow list, fed from the registry.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:50.200
OS and app policy. Device policy that closes the side doors:

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:56.533
Outlook's automation guard set to deny, and the browser's remote debugging off.

00:00:56.533 --> 00:01:01.667
When the agent makes a tools call, it goes to the MCP proxy.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.933
How does the request reach the server?

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:09.900
Routing, transport bridging, the first hop off the device.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.333
Then the MCP gateway. Should this caller be allowed?

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:18.433
Identity, authorization, policy and rate limits,

00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:21.533
enforced once instead of per server.

00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:25.300
The service boundary. Can traffic reach this backend?

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.133
The network edge in front of the server.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:34.800
The MCP server. Wrapped where needed, holding an exchanged token, never the user's.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:40.400
And the tool or enterprise data: the thing the tool call actually touches.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.100
One branch off the gateway: a third-party hosted MCP server.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:50.667
A vendor's server, where its own agent acts under the user's own grant,

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:53.167
which your gateway never issued.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:58.800
Model traffic takes its own road. The agent's prompt goes to the AI gateway.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.233
Which model, which provider? Quotas and guardrails on the inference path.

00:02:04.233 --> 00:02:07.433
Behind it, the LLM providers.

00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:10.467
The control plane feeds all of it.

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:13.933
The MCP registry: what exists, and who owns it.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:19.533
It is the source of the client's allow list and the gateway's routing table.

00:02:19.533 --> 00:02:25.433
The model registry: which models are approved, fed to the AI gateway.

00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:28.967
The identity provider: OIDC, OAuth, ID-JAG.

00:02:28.967 --> 00:02:34.433
Single sign-on for the agent, and token validation for the gateway.

00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:37.233
Workload identity: which agent is calling,

00:02:37.233 --> 00:02:41.000
so the gateway knows the workload and not just the user.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.367
GitOps and admission control. No unsanctioned server lands.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:49.567
Servers are deployed from the control plane, not by hand.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:55.033
Audit and traces. The gateway and the AI gateway send their audit logs here,

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:59.367
and the client its traces, every call joined by traceparent.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:05.067
And the two red dashed lines. Outlook, reached by a script the agent wrote against

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.067
the mail client's own automation interface.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:12.867
Teams, reached through the approved browser in remote-debugging mode.

00:03:12.867 --> 00:03:14.733
Both when the gate said no.

00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:19.567
Neither touches the gateway, and the audit log stays dark along both.

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:25.967
A person, a device, an agent, one gate every call goes through, and the tools.

00:03:25.967 --> 00:03:29.500
Everything else is that gate done properly.
